# Line endings.
#
# The working tree held a mix of CRLF and LF - the repo was built on Windows
# with tools that disagreed - and that mix cost real time: an edit anchored on
# a CRLF line silently failed to match the same line written with LF.
#
# `eol=lf` checks out LF on every platform rather than deferring to whatever
# core.autocrlf happens to be on the machine doing the clone. Every tool this
# project runs (node, pnpm, expo, dart) is happy with LF on Windows, so there
# is nothing to gain from the round trip.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats, declared before anyone adds one.
#
# `text=auto` usually detects these on its own, but "usually" is how a font or
# a photograph gets corrupted by a newline conversion. The roadmap has real
# Samui photography arriving; this is here first on purpose.
*.png    binary
*.jpg    binary
*.jpeg   binary
*.webp   binary
*.gif    binary
*.ico    binary
*.pdf    binary
*.zip    binary
*.ttf    binary
*.otf    binary
*.woff   binary
*.woff2  binary
*.mp4    binary
*.db     binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs and excluded from language statistics, because
# a lockfile changing is not a change anybody reviews line by line.
pnpm-lock.yaml   linguist-generated=true -diff
pubspec.lock     linguist-generated=true -diff
